rows.explanation:
The change updates bracket_split_build_line to add a trailing comma for import statements only after the last non‑comment leaf, skipping any STANDALONE_COMMENT nodes. This fixes the AssertionError where an extra comma was inserted before a comment in a multi‑line import ("...
    ,
)" vs the expected "...
)" ).

The change updates the regex in the js_to_json function to exclude '[' or '{' from being captured as a value token (using a look‑ahead), which corrects the conversion of JavaScript objects to proper JSON. This fixes the test failure: AssertionError: '{
                "clip":{'provider':'pseudo'}
        }' != '{
                "clip":{"provider":"pseudo"}
        }'.
